{"title":"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems\">2005 AMC 12B #5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">2005 AMC 10B #8</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-foot by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-foot bathroom floor is tiled with square tiles of size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot.  Each tile has a pattern consisting of four white quarter circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> foot centered at each corner of the tile.  The remaining portion of the tile is shaded.  How many square feet of the floor are shaded?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbe2bb4966beb1c1cbc889938c8e120b7d80639b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); fill(unitsquare,gray); filldraw(Arc((0,0),.5,0,90)--(0,0)--cycle,white,black); filldraw(Arc((1,0),.5,90,180)--(1,0)--cycle,white,black); filldraw(Arc((1,1),.5,180,270)--(1,1)--cycle,white,black); filldraw(Arc((0,1),.5,270,360)--(0,1)--cycle,white,black); [/asy]\" width=\"98\" height=\"98\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d953ba9d249c20aa4700d32d3d861407f59f7ccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\ 80-20\\pi      \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\ 60-10\\pi      \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\ 80-10\\pi      \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\ 60+10\\pi      \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\ 80+10\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"685\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> tiles.  Each tile has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/617c9a81577193c333f0b80c64514805a1e55857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\mbox{square} - 4 \\cdot (\\mbox{quarter circle})]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" /> shaded.  Thus:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/196e2b269a7dde966c160cf65bde833a9d4a2840.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\mbox{shaded area} &amp;= 80 \\left( 1 - 4 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{4} \\cdot \\pi \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^2\\right) \\\\ &amp;= 80\\left(1-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\pi\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }80-20\\pi}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"305\" height=\"137\" />\n4 quarters of a circle is a circle so that may save you 0.5 seconds&#160;:)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B\">2005 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 10